---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { outsideOfWork } from '../data/resume';
import headshot from '../assets/headshot.jpg';
---

<Base
  title="About — Pranav Gillella"
  description="Carrollton, Texas to UIUC. Why I'm studying finance and computer science together, and what I'm building toward."
>
  <Section title="About" as="h1" gap="tight">
    {/* Square and sharp-edged: the site has no rounded corners. See DESIGN.md §5. */}
    <Image
      class="portrait"
      src={headshot}
      alt="Pranav Gillella"
      width={440}
      height={440}
      loading="eager"
    />
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I grew up in Carrollton, Texas, and I'm a freshman at the University of
        Illinois — finance in Gies, computer science minor in Grainger.
      </p>
      <p>
        Markets came first — in 2023 I won the Stock Market Game and was a
        national finalist in InvestWrite. What stuck wasn't the winning. It was
        that an argument about a company could be checked against what happened
        next. Code came second, through AP Computer Science, and it's the same
        instinct: make the claim, then find out whether you were right.
      </p>
      <p>
        So I do both. Finance without programming means taking someone else's
        numbers on faith; programming without finance means building tools with
        no view of what's worth measuring.
      </p>
      <p>
        I run Quant Labs LLC — two products I built and operate alone. EarlyDMV
        rebooks Texas DPS driver license appointments into earlier slots.
        Protestly files Denton County property tax protests and argues them at
        the appraisal review board. Both are live, both have paying customers,
        both on hardware I manage myself.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm working toward quant research or trading. The <a
          href="/projects/ma-crossover-backtest">backtester</a
        > is where that starts — I wrote the metrics from scratch to understand
        what they hide.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Outside of work" gap="tight">
    <ul class="plain">
      {outsideOfWork.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section gap="tight">
    {/* A sentence, so the links keep their underlines. */}
    <p class="prose">
      More detail on <a href="/experience">experience and skills</a>, or the <a
        href="/resume">résumé</a
      >.
    </p>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  .portrait {
    display: block;
    width: 220px;
    height: auto;
    max-width: 100%;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
</style>
